From 5c7c64af06c13bd82b719944527fb9b3996980e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:08:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 169/206] F142: stop the F135 skip-window comment overclaiming
 external branches

The comment said every branch DecodeBranchDelta accepts, "local or
external", is handled inside the pool-load skip window. Probe rows
N7/N7b-d/N7f (reports_20260925/f135_window_patch_probe.py) show a
conditional branch (b.cond/cbz) whose target lies outside the function
still hashes differently from theirs, in or out of the window. State
what is measured (local b/bl/b.cond/cbz/tbz, external b/bl) and leave a
TODO for the external-conditional gap. Comment-only change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/analyze_snapshot_api_impl.cc b/runtime/vm/analyze_snapshot_api_impl.cc
index 3642ef75927..8120927b1e1 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/analyze_snapshot_api_impl.cc
+++ b/runtime/vm/analyze_snapshot_api_impl.cc
@@ -1497,13 +1497,18 @@ ShorebirdCodeFacts ComputeShorebirdCodeFacts(const uint8_t* code,
       //    both sides -- the fixed 3-n budget itself matches theirs (this is
       //    also why the F68 self_pp slots are a codegen-layout effect, not an
       //    over-eager decoder: their analyzer carries the same skip);
-      //  * but a DIRECT BRANCH (anything DecodeBranchDelta accepts: b, bl, b.cond,
-      //    local or external) inside the window is still classified, and it does
-      //    NOT spend the budget: `bl` at word 5 hashes identically to `bl` at
-      //    word 7 with 5-6 left as NOPs (their self_hash d539947c both ways),
-      //    i.e. the window slides past the branch and swallows word 7 instead.
+      //  * but a DIRECT BRANCH (anything DecodeBranchDelta accepts) inside the
+      //    window is handed to classify_branch and does NOT spend the budget:
+      //    `bl` at word 5 hashes identically to `bl` at word 7 with 5-6 left as
+      //    NOPs (their self_hash d539947c both ways), i.e. the window slides
+      //    past the branch and swallows word 7 instead. Measured to match
+      //    theirs for local b/bl/b.cond/cbz/tbz and for external b/bl.
       // Before this, ours swallowed the branch too: callees [19] vs their
       // [19,25], self_hash c9dafe74 vs d539947c.
+      // TODO(F135/N7): NOT handled -- a CONDITIONAL branch (b.cond/cbz) whose
+      // target is outside the function. classify_branch records it as kRaw and
+      // self_hash still differs from theirs, inside the window or not (probe
+      // rows N7, N7b-d, N7f). Pre-existing, out of F135 scope, still open.
       facts.classified.push_back({ShorebirdClassifiedStep::kPool, used, index});
 #if F67_POOL_SEEN_DEDUP
       if (pool_seen.insert(index).second) facts.pool_indices.push_back(index);
-- 
